def is_leap_year(year):
    if year % 400 == 0:
        return True
    elif year % 100 == 0:
        return False
    else:
        return year % 4 == 0
```

This function now correctly implements the rules for determining whether a year is a leap year. It first checks if the year is divisible by 400, in which case it is a leap year. If not, it checks if the year is divisible by 100, in which case it is not a leap year. If neither of these conditions is true, it checks if the year is divisible by 4, in which case it is a leap year.
